{"id": "00001514-0000-4000-8000-000000001514", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"text": "I'll review your RDS instances and Aurora clusters for best practices, with a focus on backup configuration. I'm checking retention, deletion protection, Multi-AZ, encryption, and similar settings across the associated accounts and regions. I'll report back when the review is done.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "tooluse_GOzbO3YZBqWV0evcgqt8S6", "tool_name": "subagent", "input": {"name": "rds-aurora-best-practices-review", "agent_type": "generic", "prompt": "{
  "task": "Review all RDS DB instances and Aurora DB clusters for best-practices compliance and backup configuration. READ-ONLY: do not make any changes.",
  "context": "User asked: 'Review my RDS instances and Aurora clusters for best practices compliance and backup configuration'. This is a survey/audit, not a root-cause hunt. Start with the agent space's own account (123456789012) in us-east-1, and use list_associations to find other associated AWS accounts. Check the regions where RDS resources exist (check us-east-1 first, then other commonly used regions such as us-east-2, us-west-2, eu-west-1; use describe calls to find where resources exist).",
  "resources": ["RDS DB instances (describe_db_instances)", "Aurora/Multi-AZ DB clusters (describe_db_clusters)", "DB snapshots / cluster snapshots", "AWS Backup plans/selections covering RDS/Aurora (if available)", "DB parameter groups, subnet groups, event subscriptions"],
  "timeframe": "Current state; for snapshots look at the last ~30 days",
  "criteria": "For each instance and cluster, assess: (1) Backup: BackupRetentionPeriod (flag 0 = disabled, and <7 days), PreferredBackupWindow, automated snapshot existence/recency, latest restorable time, manual snapshots, copy-tags-to-snapshot, cross-region backup replication / AWS Backup coverage, Aurora backtrack where applicable; (2) Availability: Multi-AZ (instances), Aurora cluster with 2+ instances across AZs, failover readiness; (3) Protection: DeletionProtection, final-snapshot-on-delete; (4) Security: StorageEncrypted/KMS, PubliclyAccessible, IAM database authentication, SSL/TLS enforcement via parameter group (rds.force_ssl), security group openness (0.0.0.0/0 on DB ports), secrets management via Secrets Manager (ManageMasterUserPassword); (5) Operations: AutoMinorVersionUpgrade, engine version currency / end-of-support or extended support, CA certificate expiry, Performance Insights, Enhanced Monitoring, CloudWatch Logs exports, maintenance window, event subscriptions, gp2 vs gp3 storage, instance class generation. Produce a concise summary: counts of resources reviewed, a table of findings per resource with severity (High/Medium/Low), and the top prioritized recommendations. Highlight backup-related gaps first. Be honest about anything you could not check (e.g. permission errors). Keep output concise."
}"}, "type": "tool_use", "display_intent": "Review RDS and Aurora best practices and backups"}], "created_at": null}

